{
  "id": "the-tilt",
  "name": "The Tilt",
  "description": "The Tilt, a cheap late-night bar down the Ribbon from Hae's, in a building that settled years ago so the whole floor runs downhill toward the back wall; the owners never leveled it. The stools in front of the long battered bar are bolted down and the glasses are heavy-bottomed. Behind the bar: shelves of cheap bottles, a row of taps, an old register, a lit drinks fridge and three small monitors running static and grainy pictures, under three pendant lamps and an orange neon sign of a tipped-over glass. At the bar's end, a plain wooden staff door under a small caged lamp, a scarf on the hook beside it: the way up to Cass's room. Worn red booths with a candle on the table, an old arcade cabinet that still takes coins, and a tall window full of Ribbon towers. Couriers, shift workers and workers from three different houses drink here, each to their own tables; there's a rule against settling business inside, and the staff enforce it. Cass works the late shift.",
